---
LLMD serves model inference to clients. Running the server and connecting to an
existing server are separate starting points.

# [Start a server]($heading.id('start-a-server'))

Serve a model and send a chat request with the
[CUDA quickstart]($link.page('llmd/quickstart')) for Docker or the
[Apple Silicon quickstart]($link.page('llmd/quickstart-apple-silicon')) for Homebrew.
See the [CLI reference]($link.page('llmd/cli')) for server flags and Docker options,
and [Supported Models]($link.page('llmd/models')) to find a checkpoint and launch
recipe for your hardware.
Use [Docker launch]($link.page('llmd/launch')) to configure a startup command
for a downloaded checkpoint or a Hugging Face repository.

A complete first-run procedure needs a compatible installation, an accessible
model, an explicit model name, and a readiness check. Success means receiving a
model response, not just observing that the process has started.

# [Connect an application]($heading.id('connect-an-application'))

Identify the server endpoint and exposed model name before sending a request.
The client and server must agree on the request format and model identifier.
Use the [API reference]($link.page('llmd/api')) to list the loaded model,
send chat requests, and read streaming responses.

# [Operate the service]($heading.id('operate-the-service'))

Continue to [Operations]($link.page('operations')) for deployment concerns, or
[compare the ecosystem projects]($link.page('start')) to choose another path.
